00:00:00,04 --> 00:00:02,06
- [Instructor] useEffect is another React hook

2
00:00:02,06 --> 00:00:05,01
that lets you apply side effects on every render

3
00:00:05,01 --> 00:00:08,03
based on the latest props and a previous state.

4
00:00:08,03 --> 00:00:10,01
useEffect takes two parameters,

5
00:00:10,01 --> 00:00:12,09
a callback function and a list of dependencies.

6
00:00:12,09 --> 00:00:15,08
This allows to apply side effects whenever there is a change

7
00:00:15,08 --> 00:00:17,09
in the state within the components.

8
00:00:17,09 --> 00:00:20,02
In our example, we want to verify

9
00:00:20,02 --> 00:00:22,09
if the user input matches two values added together,

10
00:00:22,09 --> 00:00:25,04
then apply side effects based on the results

11
00:00:25,04 --> 00:00:28,02
based on whether the answer is right or wrong.

12
00:00:28,02 --> 00:00:30,05
Back in Codespaces, I made some changes

13
00:00:30,05 --> 00:00:33,04
and decided to include parts of the code into components

14
00:00:33,04 --> 00:00:37,02
to make the code better organized into multiple components.

15
00:00:37,02 --> 00:00:39,08
This is a key feature of the React library

16
00:00:39,08 --> 00:00:41,05
which is called composition,

17
00:00:41,05 --> 00:00:45,03
which is to divide and organize the UI into small units.

18
00:00:45,03 --> 00:00:48,03
