118
00:05:23,07 --> 00:05:25,02
It is important to understand

119
00:05:25,02 --> 00:05:27,02
what is declarative programming,

120
00:05:27,02 --> 00:05:28,06
which is a high-level concept

121
00:05:28,06 --> 00:05:30,07
that expresses the logic of a program

122
00:05:30,07 --> 00:05:33,03
without specifying the control flow,

123
00:05:33,03 --> 00:05:34,08
meaning that instead of describing

124
00:05:34,08 --> 00:05:37,06
how a task should be performed step by step,

125
00:05:37,06 --> 00:05:41,05
it focuses on describing the what and the desired outcome.

126
00:05:41,05 --> 00:05:43,03
This is what we do in our example.

127
00:05:43,03 --> 00:05:46,03
We run the program and manage the state with the hooks,

128
00:05:46,03 --> 00:05:47,08
then we apply the side effects

129
00:05:47,08 --> 00:05:51,01
based on the state passed to child components.

130
00:05:51,01 --> 00:05:53,09
So we tell the program when to apply the side effects,

131
00:05:53,09 --> 00:05:55,07
meaning that we apply the side effects

132
00:05:55,07 --> 00:05:58,02
whenever there is a change in the states.

133
00:05:58,02 --> 00:06:01,01
So now we see that the application is growing really fast.

